# Lets vaultd write the synced vault copy (docs/sync.md, "Sync under systemd").
# vaultd.service makes the whole file system read-only except its own
# folders, so a copy in ~/Dropbox or ~/OneDrive cannot be merged or saved.
#
# User service:
#   systemctl --user edit vaultd
# and paste the lines below (change the folder), then
#   systemctl --user restart vaultd
#
# System service (vaultd@.service also hides /home, so name the folder in
# both lines; the folder must be readable by the "vault" user):
#   sudo systemctl edit vaultd@$USER
[Service]
ReadWritePaths=%h/Dropbox
# System service only:
# BindPaths=/home/alex/Dropbox
